[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2468904234","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/99074#issuecomment-2468904234","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99074","id":2468904234,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6TKH0q","user":{"login":"PhairZ","id":123702514,"node_id":"U_kgDOB1-M8g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/123702514?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ","html_url":"https://github.com/PhairZ","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhairZ/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-11T19:42:47Z","updated_at":"2024-11-11T19:42:47Z","body":"This is because Orthogonal view doesn't behave the same way Prespective view does.\r\n\r\nwhat  would you propose be the behaviour of Align Transform with View on Camera3D.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2468904234/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2468998286","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/99074#issuecomment-2468998286","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99074","id":2468998286,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6TKeyO","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-11T20:49:50Z","updated_at":"2024-11-11T20:50:02Z","body":"> This is because Orthogonal view doesn't behave the same way Prespective view does.\r\n\r\nI didn't notice @ydeltastar was specifically referring to orthogonal mode in the proposal.\r\n\r\nIndeed, it's probably more difficult to adapt this behavior to orthogonal mode. It should still be possible somewhat to take the camera's panning into account at least, but its local Z positioning is difficult to determine. It could be based on the orthogonal size property but I don't think a standard way to translate it exists.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2468998286/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2469338001","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/99074#issuecomment-2469338001","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99074","id":2469338001,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6TLxuR","user":{"login":"ydeltastar","id":133662278,"node_id":"U_kgDOB_eGRg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/133662278?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar","html_url":"https://github.com/ydeltastar","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-12T00:18:27Z","updated_at":"2024-11-12T00:39:18Z","body":"> Indeed, it's probably more difficult to adapt this behavior to orthogonal mode. It should still be possible somewhat to take the camera's panning into account at least, but its local Z positioning is difficult to determine.\r\n\r\nIt is simple because the 3D navigation is implemented as a cursor position and a distance from it. The math is just `node.position = cursor.position + camera.basis.z * cursor.distance` and `node.basis = camera.basis`.\r\n\r\nResult:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/3ba97584-9a55-4b1d-a9b8-c39d26c7adde\r\n\r\n\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2469338001/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]